    "status": "on_track",
    "notes": "Every muscle group improved its strength index this period. Legs led the way with a jump from 105 to 110, followed by glutes (104 to 108) and back (103 to 107). Chest moved from 102 to 106, while shoulders (102 to 103) and core (101 to 102) showed smaller but still positive gains. This is a clean sweep of progressive overload across the entire session, and it continues the upward trend noted last period. The smaller gains in shoulders and core are normal given their relatively lower volume, and they are still moving in the right direction."
