    "Add one extra set of direct shoulder work, such as lateral raises or face pulls, to close the gap between shoulder volume and the rest of your upper body and protect joint health over the long term.",
    "Continue monitoring recovery between sessions. You are training effectively and progressing on all fronts, so protecting sleep and managing stress outside the gym will be key to sustaining this trajectory at age 46."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "All six muscle groups achieved strength index gains this period, with legs and glutes leading progress; mild imbalances in core and shoulder volume are the only areas to address going forward."
}
